# The Aether release fbs-core is built and tested against.
#
# A FLOOR, not a preference: the oldest Aether that can compile this
# repo's sources and run its suite. Anything newer on PATH is used as-is.
#
# Why 0.542.0 — the port's test suite is `std.spec` (+
# `std.http.client.httptest`), the stdlib absorption of the retired
# aeocha framework. `std.spec` landed in 0.538.0 and the process/HTTP
# matcher modules alongside it, so 0.538.0 is the language floor; we pin
# to 0.542.0 because that is the release the suite is verified green on,
# and because 0.541.0 carries the weak-`aether_lib_meta` fix that aeb's
# multi-TU `--emit=lib` link shape needs (see aeb's own AETHER_PIN).
#
# Bump when this repo starts calling a primitive an older Aether lacks.
#
# Raised 0.542.0 -> 0.778.0 (2026-10-05). A TRACKING/policy move to the
# family-wide floor every Aether repo moved to the same day -- but one that
# the code now genuinely needs, because the port had to change to build:
#
#   1. Aether 0.758 (#2301): the byte-payload std calls take a `byte[]` slice
#      (the length travels with it) instead of (ptr/string, len) pairs.
#      fbs-core calls the slice forms of fs.write_atomic / fs.pwrite,
#      cryptography.md5_hex / sha256_hex / hmac_sha256_hex /
#      hmac_sha256_bytes / digest_update and http client set_body
#      (string.bytes(s), or string.aether_string_raw_ptr(p) as byte[] bounded
#      by an explicit length where the body is http.request_body's raw char*
#      that can hold NULs), so it CANNOT COMPILE below 0.758.
#   2. 0.612: spec.run_summary returns its verdict instead of exiting; the
#      suites now `return spec.run_summary(fw)` so a failing spec exits
#      non-zero (the bare call was measured exiting 0 on a failing spec).
#      On an ae below 0.612 that return hands main() garbage.
#   3. 0.741 (#2208): release installs ship contrib/, so `import
#      contrib.sqlite` resolves from a get.sh toolchain with no aether source
#      checkout. (The veneer archive it links, -laether_sqlite, is still not
#      shipped: scripts/sqlite_veneer.sh builds it from that contrib source.)
#
# So the code's own minimum is now 0.758.0; 0.778.0 is the family floor and
# the release it is verified on (macOS arm64): ./build.sh builds the server,
# scripts/aetest.sh runs all 19 suites green (94 specs + large_sizes, the
# same as 0.542.0 gave on the pre-port code), and a real server round trip
# (bootstrap, bucket, PUT/GET/HEAD/LIST/copy/multipart/DELETE) matches 0.542.
#
# Raised 0.778.0 -> 0.823.0 (2026-10-17). Again a family-wide move (Paul:
# the whole family on 0.823.0), and again one the code needs:
#
#   4. 0.818 (#2926): a `ptr` parameter a function keeps must say
#      `@keep ptr` (E0902). s3server.set_state stores the sqlite handle in
#      the AppCtx it returns, so it is `db: @keep ptr`, which no Aether
#      before 0.818 parses. The code's own minimum is now 0.818.0.
#
# Verified on 0.823.0 (macOS arm64, aether-linux arm64, ae-x64 gcc
# -Werror): scripts/aetest.sh runs all 19 suites green (94 specs +
# large_sizes), ./build.sh builds the server, and a live round trip
# (bootstrap, bucket, PUT/GET of a NUL-bearing body, HEAD, LIST, copy,
# DELETE, 404 after delete) behaves. ./build.sh needs an aeb newer than
# v0.326 (see AEB_PIN).
#
# Raised 0.823.0 -> 0.824.0 (2026-10-18). A TRACKING bump with the family,
# not one the code needs (its own minimum stays 0.818.0): nothing here is
# named like a generated helper (now under _aether_) or spawn_<Actor>, and no
# closure keeps a slice of its frame (0.824's new E0900 cases). Verified on
# 0.824.0 built from its tag, with aeb v0.327 (macOS arm64, aether-linux
# arm64, ae-x64 gcc -Werror): scripts/aetest.sh runs all 19 suites green (94
# specs + large_sizes), ./build.sh builds the server with no C warnings, and
# the same live round trip behaves (bytes identical, 404 after delete).
#
# Raised 0.824.0 -> 0.931.0 (2026-11-20). A FLOOR MOVE: the code had to change
# for 0.931.0, and none of it builds on the old pin. What 0.931.0 forced:
#
#   5. `string.aether_string_raw_ptr` is no longer exported from std.string
#      (E0303). The three sites that bounded a raw pointer by hand now use
#      `string.bytes(s)[0..n]` for owned strings, and the multipart part
#      handler takes `http.request_body_bytes(req)` (a byte[] bounded by the
#      real body length, so NULs survive) and storage.write_part takes that
#      byte[] directly.
#   6. `http.request_body_length` returns a long, so the streaming PUT's
#      running offset is declared `long off` (E0200, narrowing).
#   7. `fs.file_close` became `fs.close` (0.850.0), which also returns the
#      close error; storage.stream_finish now reports it.
#
# The code's own minimum is therefore 0.931.0 for item 5 alone; it is the
# release this is verified on. Verified on 0.931.0 with aeb v0.348 (Linux
# x86_64, cachyos): scripts/aetest.sh runs all 19 suites green (94 specs),
# ./build.sh builds the server, and a live round trip (bootstrap, bucket,
# PUT/GET/HEAD of a NUL-bearing body, a 512000-byte streamed body and an empty
# body, a two-part multipart upload with NULs, DELETE, 404 after delete) gives
# byte-identical bodies and ETags equal to the md5 of the bytes. The build
# also links on macOS arm64. Not run: the live server on macOS, the old
# platforms of earlier bumps (aether-linux arm64, ae-x64 gcc -Werror).
# Raised 0.931.0 -> 0.935.0 (2026-11-22): a tracking-only bump, no new primitive
# needed and no source change. Verified on ae-x64 (Ubuntu 22.04 x86_64): scripts/aetest.sh, 94 specs
# green, and ./build.sh builds the server (no live round trip).
# Raised 0.935.0 -> 0.936.0 (2026-11-22): a tracking-only bump, no new primitive
# needed and no source change. Verified on ae-x64 (Ubuntu 22.04 x86_64): scripts/aetest.sh, 94 specs
# green, and ./build.sh builds the server (no live round trip).
# Raised 0.936.0 -> 0.939.0 (2026-11-23): a tracking-only bump, no new primitive
# needed and no source change (nothing here uses the removed std.http.client
# process-wide pool). Verified on ae-x64 (Ubuntu 22.04 x86_64) with a 0.939.0
# release install: scripts/aetest.sh, 94 specs green, and ./build.sh builds the
# server (no live round trip).
